WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.552
A common table expression is useful when one stage deserves a name.

00:00:04.552 --> 00:00:08.132
It can make a multi-step query easier to read.

00:00:08.132 --> 00:00:15.002
It is especially helpful when you need to calculate a window value first and filter that result later.

00:00:15.002 --> 00:00:19.972
Recursive queries also use the common table expression structure.

00:00:19.972 --> 00:00:26.823
Use a common table expression because it clarifies the logic, not simply because the query is long.
